{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.JonesViaMarkovTrace","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.JonesViaMarkovTrace","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Braiding.HnMarkovTrace"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesViaMarkovTrace.lean#L62-L74","doc":"**The Hopf-link Jones value is positive** in the Wenzl regime (`q > 1`):\nunder convention D the closed form is `(q⁴ + 1)/(q² + 1)`, a ratio of\nmanifestly positive reals, so `positivity` closes it outright.\n\nThe convention-C proof needed `q^{5/2} ≥ q^{1/2}` via\n`Real.rpow_le_rpow_of_exponent_le` and then `nlinarith`, because the numerator\nwas a *difference* of half-powers whose sign had to be argued. Convention D\nhas no subtraction and no square roots. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesViaMarkovTrace.lean#L49-L60","doc":"**Closed form of the Hopf-link Jones value** in the canonical instance\n(`q > 1`), **convention D**: `J(Hopf) = (q⁴ + 1) / (q² + 1)`.\n\n**Migrated 2026-08-26 (bean `qou-cxjq`)** with `markovTraceTower_canonical`.\nThis read `(q^{5/2} − q^{1/2} + q² + q) / (q² + q)`, the convention-C value,\nand was proved by `rfl` off the instance's `trM_sigma1_sq` field. Because it\nis `rfl` against a field of that instance, it MUST move whenever the instance\ndoes — a `rfl` closed form is exactly as convention-bound as the instance it\nunfolds, however convention-free its own statement looks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf_invariant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf_invariant","kind":"theorem","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesViaMarkovTrace.lean#L38-L47","doc":"**The Jones value is a link invariant.** The Markov trace of `σ_1²` computed\nin any `H_n(q)` with `n ≥ 2` agrees with the base `H_2` value `jonesHopf`,\nby Markov stabilisation (`σ_1²` uses only the first generator, so extra\nstrands contribute `z · z⁻¹ = 1`). This is exactly the property that makes\nthe Markov trace descend to a knot/link invariant (Jones 1987). Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.jonesHopf","kind":"def","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/JonesViaMarkovTrace.lean#L32-L36","doc":"**Jones value of the Hopf link**, via the Markov trace on the `H_n(q)`\ntower: `J(Hopf) = tr_M(σ_1²)`, evaluated at the base strand count `n = 2`\n(the `σ_1²`-closure is the Hopf link, `BraidLinkTypes.closure2`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}